{"id":"e0a8c12c-bcc2-4673-b580-4718d1cae9b5","object":"chat.completion","created":1784958125,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = case['required_symbols']\\n    node_by_id = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children_of = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n['parent'] is not None:\\n            children_of[n['parent']].append(n['id'])\\n    all_symbols = [n['symbol'] for n in nodes]\\n    for rs in required_symbols:\\n        if rs not in all_symbols:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Required symbol {rs} not found in any node\\\")\\n    retained_ids = set(node_by_id.keys())\\n    removed_ids = []\\n    symbol_count = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        s = n['symbol']\\n        symbol_count[s] = symbol_count.get(s, 0) + 1\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        if nid not in retained_ids:\\n            continue\\n        if not n['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        if n['parent'] is None:\\n            continue\\n        has_retained_child = False\\n        for cid in children_of.get(nid, []):\\n            if cid in retained_ids:\\n                has_retained_child = True\\n                break\\n        if has_retained_child:\\n            continue\\n        sym = n['symbol']\\n        can_remove = True\\n        for rs in required_symbols:\\n            if symbol_count.get(rs, 0) - (1 if rs == sym else 0) < 1:\\n                can_remove = False\\n                break\\n        if can_remove:\\n            removed_ids.append(nid)\\n            retained_ids.remove(nid)\\n            symbol_count[sym] = symbol_count.get(sym, 0) - 1\\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained_ids)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_ids,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": retained_sorted\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that returns {\"removed_node_ids\": [...], \"retained_node_ids\": [...]}. The task is grammar-guided node reduction. The input case has nodes with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility. Also has required_symbols.\n\nThe algorithm: We need to reduce the tree by removing removable nodes while preserving required symbols and grammar validity? The description says \"grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates\" but we have no grammar rules. Actually, the problem is about Perses syntax-guided reduction. But given the schema, we have nodes with parent relationships. The required_symbols are symbols that must remain. Also, we cannot remove a node if it has retained children? Actually, we need to consider deeper nodes first.\n\nObjective: Remove as many removable nodes as possible while ensuring that the remaining tree contains all required symbols and is \"grammar-valid\"? Since we have no grammar, we probably just need to ensure that the tree structure is maintained (i.e., parent-child relationships) and that required symbols are present.\n\nGiven the public fixtures, we see a tree where root is required, s1 is required. Some nodes are removable. The result must list removed_node_ids and retained_node_ids.\n\nWe need to decide which nodes to remove. The description: \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" So we try to remove removable nodes, but only if after removal, all required symbols are still present in the retained tree. Also, we consider deeper nodes first.\n\nWe need to implement a traversal that processes nodes in order of decreasing depth, and for nodes at same depth, stable tie break by node ID. We'll attempt to remove each removable node, but before removing, check if any required symbol would be missing? Actually, removing a node only removes that node itself. But if a node's descendants are still there, they might still provide the symbols? But if we remove a node, its children become orphans? In a tree, if we remove a node, we must also remove its descendants? Or can we keep children? The description: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" So we cannot remove a node if it has any children that are retained. That implies that removing a node removes it and all its descendants? Actually, \"node with retained children\" means if we decide to keep some children, we cannot remove the parent? More likely, the reduction process removes subtrees. When a node is removed, all its descendants are also removed because the tree is pruned. So we need to consider that removing a node removes the entire subtree rooted at that node.\n\nTherefore, we need to decide which subtrees to remove. The goal is to remove as many removable nodes as possible while keeping the required symbols present in the remaining tree.\n\nAlgorithm: Build a tree from nodes. For each node, we can compute the set of symbols in its subtree. Then, we want to find a set of nodes to remove such that after removal, the remaining forest (or tree rooted at root) contains all required symbols, and we remove as many nodes as possible. But the problem says \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" So we can try to remove nodes in order of depth (deepest first) and see if removing that node (and its subtree) still leaves all required symbols somewhere else in the tree. If yes, we remove it. If not, we keep it.\n\nBut we must also consider \"never remove ... a node with retained children.\" That implies if we decide to keep some children, we cannot remove the parent. So the process is: from bottom up, we decide to prune subtrees. For each node, we check if we can remove it (i.e., it is removable) and if removing its entire subtree does not cause any required symbol to be missing from the rest of the tree (including ancestors and siblings). Since we process deeper